          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP384 - Hinton - Bradwell

Posted: N53 24.222 W117 32.982

MyGPSr: N53 24.222 W117 32.983&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Found it 1 foot SE of the metal guard post near two big rocks. It was 1 inch below ground level and didn't need any cleaning. Thanks for the cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="319227210">
          <groundspeak:date>2013-06-01T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP384 Hinton Bradwell&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MyGPSr:  N53 24.221 W117 32.983

Elevation: 1043 m&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This was a comical finding session. First I parked a little too far away at first and after making my way over to find the marker post, as seeing I'd have to do some digging, I reparked and brought over a few tools. I took a nearby hole beside the post to be the home of the cap and starting digging away at that only to find, LOTS of rocks masquerading as caps. Then I poked a few inches closer to the post from that hold in a different spot and found... a cap. Sheesh. Both the parking and find had to be re-adjusted just a bit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="214648421">
          <groundspeak:date>2012-02-22T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="664594">Sears Tower</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP384 - Hinton - Bradwell&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The last one of the night!  Time to drive back to Edson and have some late dinner.  TFTH!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="191906594">
          <groundspeak:date>2011-10-07T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="228846">Mr. CanoeHead</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP384 Hinton-Bradwell

The residents here appear to be able to access the ATV trails rigth from their neighbourhood.  Lucky for us they weren't taking advantage of this luxury as we got the numbers from the cap without being run over by any ATV's.  TFCap&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
